      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "All of the above",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BF</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> is a Lewis acid, as it accepts lone pair of electrons.</p><p>It is not an Arrhenius acid because it does not furnish <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math> ion in its aqueous solution.</p><p>It is also not a Bronsted Lowry acid as if does not give <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;ions in any solvent.</p></blockquote>"
  }
